13. Move Zeros to the End
-------------------------
Input: [0, 1, 0, 3, 12]
Output: [1, 3, 12, 0, 0]

Two-pointer style
        int[] arr = {0, 1, 0, 3, 12};
        int index = 0;
        for (int num : arr) {
            if (num != 0) {
                arr[index] = num;
                index++;
            }
        }
        
        while (index < arr.length) {
            arr[index] = 0;
            index++;
        }
        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(arr));

Understand the logic
        First:
                [0, 1, 0, 3, 12]
                    ↓
                [1, 3, 12, ?, ?]
        Then fill remaining positions with zero:
                [1, 3, 12, 0, 0]
        Pattern: Put valid elements first → fill remaining positions with zero.

14. Find Pair Whose Sum Equals Target
-------------------------------------
Input: arr = [2, 7, 11, 15]
target = 9
Output: 2 + 7 = 9

Using HashSet
    int[] arr = {2, 7, 11, 15};
    int target = 9;

    Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
    for (int num : arr) {
        int required = target - num;
        if (set.contains(required)) {
            System.out.println(
                required + " + " + num + " = " + target
            );
            break;
        }
        set.add(num);
    }

Understand the key idea
    For: target = 9 num = 7
    we calculate:
    required = 9 - 7  = 2
    Then ask: set.contains(2)


